      "claim": "Therefore, having \"lots of chlorophyll\" is not required—and can be detrimental—to the appearance of many hostas that look their best when chlorophyll is limited to the green portions of the leaf.",
      "evidence": "If chlorophyll were increased throughout the leaf, the characteristic variegation or blue‑green hue would be reduced, making the plant less attractive according to the standards in step 3.",
